<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vatsaraja</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 780–800</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vatsaraja was a king of the Gurjara-Pratihara dynasty in the late 8th century who made it a major power in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. He defeated the Pala king Dharmapala in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> valley but was then beaten by the Rashtrakuta king Dhruva, in the first round of the long tripartite struggle for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a>. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagabhata-ii">Nagabhata II</a> took Kannauj and made it the capital.</p></div>
